WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.150
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.420 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.470 --> 01:37.890
[Episode 20]

4
01:41.350 --> 01:43.680
While the Zunyi Conference was underway,

5
01:44.150 --> 01:45.350
the 10th Red Army Corps

6
01:45.350 --> 01:49.080
having suffered repeated defeats after the Battle of Tanjiaqiao,

7
01:49.390 --> 01:54.080
was forced to retreat south from the Anhui-Jiangxi border region toward northeastern Jiangxi.

8
01:54.080 --> 01:54.880
En route,

9
01:54.900 --> 01:56.650
it was intercepted by KMT troops

10
01:56.650 --> 01:58.650
at Gangtou Village in Dexing County

11
01:59.130 --> 02:01.210
and split into two sections.

12
02:01.640 --> 02:02.880
The troops were then surrounded

13
02:02.880 --> 02:05.880
by enemy forces in the Huaiyu Mountains.

14
02:05.400 --> 02:10.550
[Huaiyu Mountains, Jiangxi]

15
02:23.360 --> 02:24.240
Chairman Fang.

16
02:24.680 --> 02:25.880
How is the situation?

17
02:25.890 --> 02:26.730
The reconnaissance is complete.

18
02:26.640 --> 02:29.960
[Su Yu, Chief of Staff of the 10th Red Army Corps]

19
02:27.010 --> 02:28.960
The enemy's encirclement is not yet fully closed.

20
02:28.960 --> 02:30.680
We have a chance if we break out overnight.

21
02:30.530 --> 02:34.530
[Fang Zhimin, Chairman of the Military and Political Committee of the 10th Red Army Corps]

22
02:30.840 --> 02:31.800
Great.

23
02:34.240 --> 02:36.079
This is the enemy's last blockade.

24
02:36.079 --> 02:36.930
If we break through,

25
02:36.930 --> 02:38.810
we can return to the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Soviet Area.

26
02:38.810 --> 02:39.610
Yes.

27
02:42.079 --> 02:42.770
I have sent someone

28
02:42.770 --> 02:44.079
back to notify Comrade Liu Chouxi,

29
02:44.079 --> 02:46.050
asking them to bring the main force back as soon as possible.

30
02:46.050 --> 02:47.120
Good.

31
02:50.640 --> 02:51.640
Chairman Fang!

32
02:52.520 --> 02:53.380
Chairman Fang!

33
02:57.360 --> 02:58.360
Why did you come back alone?

34
02:58.360 --> 02:59.240
Chairman Fang.

35
02:59.730 --> 03:01.210
The Corps Commander asked me to inform you

36
03:01.210 --> 03:03.010
that the troops are very exhausted now.

37
03:03.010 --> 03:04.360
They need to rest for the night

38
03:04.360 --> 03:06.250
and set off tomorrow during the day.

39
03:06.250 --> 03:07.220
Absolutely not.

40
03:07.760 --> 03:08.690
Chairman Fang.

41
03:09.010 --> 03:10.800
Once the enemy's encirclement is fully closed,

42
03:10.800 --> 03:12.050
with our current strength,

43
03:12.050 --> 03:13.550
it will be impossible to break out.

44
03:13.550 --> 03:15.450
I will go back to find the Commander right now.

45
03:15.450 --> 03:16.000
Guard!

46
03:16.030 --> 03:16.960
Su Yu.

47
03:17.390 --> 03:18.350
I'll go instead.

48
03:18.450 --> 03:19.310
Chairman Fang.

49
03:19.450 --> 03:20.710
I know Comrade Chouxi.

50
03:20.840 --> 03:22.079
You have already had an argument

51
03:22.079 --> 03:23.079
over the march.

52
03:23.360 --> 03:25.500
At this time, only I can persuade him.

53
03:26.960 --> 03:27.840
Chairman Fang.

54
03:28.010 --> 03:28.770
Then the comrades and I

55
03:28.770 --> 03:29.930
will wait here to meet up with you.

56
03:29.930 --> 03:31.890
No, you lead the comrades to evacuate first.

57
03:31.890 --> 03:32.770
Leave right now.

58
03:32.770 --> 03:33.630
Chairman Fang.

59
03:33.680 --> 03:34.930
If you go back at this time,

60
03:34.930 --> 03:35.800
in case you can't make it in time...

61
03:35.800 --> 03:37.640
Say no more. Execute the order.

62
03:43.400 --> 03:44.660
Our 10th Red Army Corps

63
03:44.840 --> 03:47.370
has suffered heavy losses fighting up to now.

64
03:47.610 --> 03:49.640
The enemy still has over a dozen regiments blocking us.

65
03:49.640 --> 03:51.040
When we return to the Soviet Area in the future,

66
03:51.040 --> 03:53.840
there will be even fiercer battles waiting for us.

67
03:53.990 --> 03:55.390
In the previous battles,

68
03:55.770 --> 03:58.360
comrades like Xun Huaizhou and Huang Yingte

69
03:58.360 --> 04:00.490
have already sacrificed themselves.

70
04:01.240 --> 04:02.330
Along the way,

71
04:02.520 --> 04:03.670
I have seen your capability

72
04:03.670 --> 04:05.830
in commanding battles.

73
04:05.970 --> 04:08.770
You will definitely be able to lead the comrades to a successful breakout

74
04:08.770 --> 04:10.640
and successfully lead them

75
04:10.900 --> 04:13.580
to continue fighting against the enemy.

76
04:13.640 --> 04:14.610
Comrade Fang Zhimin.

77
04:14.610 --> 04:15.210
Remember,

78
04:15.450 --> 04:17.360
never stop moving forward.

79
04:18.500 --> 04:21.500
You must lead everyone to fight the enemy to the end.

80
04:23.530 --> 04:24.880
Yes.

81
04:40.760 --> 04:41.960
Comrades.

82
04:43.050 --> 04:45.970
It's snowing heavily today.

83
04:46.610 --> 04:48.000
As the old saying goes,

84
04:48.930 --> 04:51.320
a timely snow promises a good harvest.

85
04:51.610 --> 04:53.170
By this time in previous years,

86
04:53.170 --> 04:55.120
we'd be busy preparing for the New Year,

87
04:55.120 --> 04:56.240
making cured meat

88
04:56.650 --> 04:57.970
and rice cakes

89
04:58.290 --> 05:01.490
to reward ourselves for a hard year.

90
05:01.610 --> 05:02.730
But today,

91
05:03.090 --> 05:04.530
because of the revolution,

92
05:04.530 --> 05:06.490
we stand in this freezing weather.

93
05:07.000 --> 05:08.560
I see the bloody marks on your feet

94
05:08.560 --> 05:10.970
caused by straw sandals.

95
05:10.970 --> 05:13.000
I see the scars on your bodies.

96
05:13.200 --> 05:14.610
I have them too.

97
05:15.270 --> 05:17.000
But we are still standing here.

98
05:17.320 --> 05:20.560
Because our Red Army has a will of steel.

99
05:20.760 --> 05:22.610
What does a heavy snowfall matter?

100
05:22.610 --> 05:24.930
What does this freezing cold matter?

101
05:25.000 --> 05:26.120
Snow may be cold,

102
05:26.410 --> 05:27.850
but our blood runs hot!

103
05:28.490 --> 05:29.050
I know

104
05:29.050 --> 05:30.490
we are now facing

105
05:30.800 --> 05:32.530
unprecedented difficulties.

106
05:32.680 --> 05:34.940
But this is not the time for us to despair.

107
05:35.050 --> 05:37.610
Our Red Army will not be discouraged,

108
05:37.760 --> 05:39.290
let alone pessimistic.

109
05:39.530 --> 05:41.370
Comrade Mao Zedong said,

110
05:42.400 --> 05:44.600
a single spark can start a prairie fire.

111
05:45.090 --> 05:47.680
We are those sparks

112
05:47.680 --> 05:49.530
that can start a prairie fire.

113
05:49.880 --> 05:52.440
We are the hope of the Chinese revolution.

114
05:52.560 --> 05:54.610
We must press on, following in the footsteps

115
05:54.610 --> 05:57.120
of Comrade Xun Huaizhou and all those

116
05:57.120 --> 05:58.440
who gave their lives.

117
05:59.170 --> 06:02.240
We must firmly complete the task

118
06:02.240 --> 06:03.760
assigned to us by the Party Central Committee.

119
06:03.760 --> 06:04.610
Comrades,

120
06:04.930 --> 06:07.000
for our lovely China,

121
06:07.240 --> 06:09.170
go north to resist Japan

122
06:09.170 --> 06:10.680
and continue fighting!

123
06:10.730 --> 06:12.050
Go north to resist Japan

124
06:12.050 --> 06:13.320
and continue fighting!

125
06:13.320 --> 06:14.650
Go north to resist Japan

126
06:14.650 --> 06:15.930
and continue fighting!

127
06:15.930 --> 06:17.260
Go north to resist Japan

128
06:17.320 --> 06:18.830
and continue fighting!

129
06:19.090 --> 06:20.560
Go north to resist Japan

130
06:20.610 --> 06:22.120
and continue fighting!

131
06:22.260 --> 06:23.740
Go north to resist Japan!

132
06:23.760 --> 06:25.440
Salute!

133
07:05.510 --> 07:06.910
Set off!

134
07:08.590 --> 07:09.350
That night,

135
07:09.790 --> 07:11.790
Su Yu led the vanguard

136
07:11.970 --> 07:14.530
through the enemy's blockade under the cover of darkness

137
07:14.530 --> 07:16.930
and arrived at the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Soviet Area.

138
07:16.930 --> 07:20.310
Later, they formed the Advance Division of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army,

139
07:20.310 --> 07:23.260
entered Zhejiang to carry out guerrilla warfare,

140
07:23.680 --> 07:26.550
and established the Southern Zhejiang Revolutionary Base.

141
07:26.550 --> 07:28.650
After the outbreak of the nationwide war of resistance,

142
07:28.650 --> 07:31.050
they were reorganized into the 3rd Battalion of the 4th Regiment,

143
07:31.050 --> 07:33.180
2nd Detachment of the New Fourth Army,

144
07:33.470 --> 07:35.240
and marched north to fight the Japanese.

145
07:35.240 --> 07:36.800
After Fang Zhimin returned,

146
07:36.800 --> 07:39.730
he led his troops to break out of the encirclement multiple times without success.

147
07:39.730 --> 07:41.850
Eventually, with ammunition and food exhausted,

148
07:41.850 --> 07:43.810
most of his men fell in battle.

149
07:44.570 --> 07:46.040
On January 29th,

150
07:46.120 --> 07:48.450
Fang Zhimin was unfortunately captured.

151
07:48.610 --> 07:49.409
At this point,

152
07:49.530 --> 07:52.760
the operation of the Northern Expeditionary Advance Team Against Japan failed.

153
07:52.760 --> 07:55.050
On August 6, 1935,

154
07:55.200 --> 07:58.390
Fang Zhimin died heroically in Xiashawo, Nanchang.

155
07:59.270 --> 08:01.600
During his more than six months in prison,

156
08:01.650 --> 08:03.800
Fang Zhimin wrote "Poverty",

157
08:03.820 --> 08:05.090
"Lovely China", and other manuscripts

158
08:05.090 --> 08:07.020
totaling more than 100,000 words.

159
08:07.540 --> 08:09.990
They were entrusted to someone to be taken from prison to Shanghai,

160
08:09.990 --> 08:13.390
preserved by Soong Ching-ling, Lu Xun, and others in a relay,

161
08:13.900 --> 08:15.010
and after several twists and turns,

162
08:15.010 --> 08:17.870
were finally delivered to the Party organization.

163
08:18.290 --> 08:19.560
In 1952,

164
08:19.850 --> 08:21.480
Fang Zhimin's manuscript

165
08:21.510 --> 08:23.770
Lovely China was officially published.

166
08:24.570 --> 08:25.770
In 1958,

167
08:26.090 --> 08:29.420
the remains of martyr Fang Zhimin were found and confirmed.

168
08:29.810 --> 08:31.250
In 1964,

169
08:31.570 --> 08:33.650
Mao Zedong personally wrote the inscription

170
08:33.650 --> 08:35.960
"Tomb of Martyr Fang Zhimin".

171
08:38.600 --> 08:49.120
[Qinggangpo, Tucheng, Guizhou]

172
08:41.799 --> 08:43.130
The Sichuan sun,

173
08:43.539 --> 08:44.590
the Yunnan winds,

174
08:45.330 --> 08:47.290
and Guizhou's rain all feel like winter.

175
08:47.290 --> 08:49.220
Why is it so cold even without rain?

176
08:49.770 --> 08:51.030
Tucheng is just ahead.

177
08:51.170 --> 08:51.960
After we arrive in Tucheng,

178
08:51.960 --> 08:53.480
everyone should take a good rest.

179
08:53.480 --> 08:54.530
Tucheng.

180
08:54.890 --> 08:56.370
This name is quite unique.

181
08:57.050 --> 08:58.170
This Tucheng,

182
08:58.290 --> 08:59.870
known as Zizhou in ancient times,

183
08:59.870 --> 09:02.620
is a distribution center for Sichuan salt entering Guizhou,

184
09:02.620 --> 09:05.350
and also a key point on the Northern Guizhou Road.

185
09:05.850 --> 09:07.870
If we go north out of Guizhou into Sichuan,

186
09:07.870 --> 09:10.160
this is an important passage.

187
09:10.190 --> 09:11.190
Chairman!

188
09:12.570 --> 09:13.370
Chairman!

189
09:18.220 --> 09:19.250
Vice Chairman Zhou.

190
09:19.250 --> 09:20.310
Commander-in-Chief.

191
09:20.310 --> 09:21.680
There is an urgent military situation.

192
09:21.680 --> 09:22.890
Two brigades of the Sichuan Army

193
09:22.890 --> 09:24.590
have already seized Chishui County.

194
09:24.470 --> 09:26.600
[Mao Zedong, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

195
09:24.960 --> 09:26.710
The 1st Corps' attack is blocked.

196
09:26.710 --> 09:30.190
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army and concurrently Commander of the Military Commission Column]

197
09:27.250 --> 09:28.580
The 9th Corps at Jiantan

198
09:28.720 --> 09:31.320
has also been intercepted by the Sichuan Army.

199
09:32.290 --> 09:33.480
Do we have any information on the enemy?

200
09:33.480 --> 09:34.200
Yes.

201
09:34.720 --> 09:36.290
The 5th Red Army Corps reports that

202
09:36.290 --> 09:39.680
Guo Xunqi's 3rd Training Brigade of the Sichuan Army

203
09:40.320 --> 09:43.010
and Pan Zuo's 4th Independent Brigade

204
09:43.410 --> 09:44.840
are already tailing us.

205
09:45.480 --> 09:47.170
Their vanguard is less than

206
09:47.770 --> 09:49.370
a day's journey away from us.

207
09:49.890 --> 09:52.720
Behind them is the 3rd Model Brigade,

208
09:53.010 --> 09:55.270
and Liao Ze's troops are also following.

209
09:55.650 --> 09:58.320
In addition, another regiment has already

210
09:58.570 --> 10:00.020
occupied Xishui.

211
10:00.130 --> 10:01.770
The Sichuan Army came so fast.

212
10:01.770 --> 10:02.700
This is unusual.

213
10:03.070 --> 10:03.860
Enlai,

214
10:03.750 --> 10:06.400
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission (CRMC); Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army]

215
10:04.200 --> 10:05.480
has the Second Bureau obtained

216
10:05.480 --> 10:06.800
detailed information on the Sichuan Army?

217
10:06.690 --> 10:09.450
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

218
10:07.080 --> 10:08.130
Not yet.

219
10:08.480 --> 10:10.130
Comrade Zeng Xisheng reports that

220
10:10.130 --> 10:12.480
the cipher system used by the Sichuan Army is very complex,

221
10:12.480 --> 10:14.560
and cannot be deciphered for the time being.

222
10:14.560 --> 10:16.130
The enemy situation is unclear.

223
10:16.130 --> 10:17.590
The road north is blocked,

224
10:17.680 --> 10:18.800
and the enemy is closing in.

225
10:18.800 --> 10:20.250
We risk being trapped in

226
10:20.270 --> 10:23.340
the narrow stretch between Tucheng and Chishui.

227
10:24.370 --> 10:25.290
Bocheng,

228
10:25.530 --> 10:26.290
how many troops are in the two brigades

229
10:26.290 --> 10:28.010
of Guo Xunqi and Pan Zuo

230
10:28.200 --> 10:29.080
that are hot on our heels?

231
10:29.080 --> 10:30.530
According to previous intelligence,

232
10:30.530 --> 10:33.440
the vanguard of these two brigades has a total of four regiments,

233
10:33.440 --> 10:34.840
totaling over 6,000 men,

234
10:34.840 --> 10:36.570
all under Guo Xunqi's command.

235
10:36.980 --> 10:38.010
If we concentrate

236
10:38.120 --> 10:40.290
the forces of five divisions from the 3rd and 5th Red Army Corps,

237
10:40.290 --> 10:42.600
and use the terrain to our advantage,

238
10:42.930 --> 10:45.130
do you think we have a chance of winning?

239
10:49.290 --> 10:50.080
Bocheng.

240
10:50.800 --> 10:52.960
Are you familiar with Guo Xunqi

241
10:52.960 --> 10:54.200
and his troops' fighting capabilities?

242
10:54.200 --> 10:56.080
Guo Xunqi's 3rd Training Brigade

243
10:56.530 --> 10:59.440
is considered a very capable unit in the Sichuan Army.

244
10:59.440 --> 11:00.420
This Guo Xunqi,

245
11:00.440 --> 11:01.650
nicknamed Reckless Guo,

246
11:01.650 --> 11:02.680
is a fierce general.

247
11:02.680 --> 11:03.840
During the Kuomintang-Communist cooperation,

248
11:03.840 --> 11:05.050
I had a lot of contact with him.

249
11:05.050 --> 11:05.800
At that time,

250
11:05.930 --> 11:08.080
his thinking was relatively progressive.

251
11:08.080 --> 11:08.920
Oh, right.

252
11:09.570 --> 11:13.330
He has a closer relationship with Comrade Chen Yi.

253
11:13.810 --> 11:15.260
They used to be alumni

254
11:15.560 --> 11:17.820
and even teammates on the football team.

255
11:22.370 --> 11:23.560
What is the name of this place?

256
11:23.560 --> 11:24.400
Qinggangpo.

257
11:24.610 --> 11:26.610
It's about six li away from Tucheng.

258
11:27.200 --> 11:28.050
Chairman! Mao!

259
11:28.050 --> 11:28.980
Comrade Zedong.

260
11:30.180 --> 11:31.600
We'll fight a blocking action right here.

261
11:31.600 --> 11:33.930
This is a good place for a blocking action.

262
11:33.930 --> 11:34.930
The pursuing enemy is pressing hard.

263
11:34.930 --> 11:36.890
We can consider concentrating our forces

264
11:36.890 --> 11:39.130
to take the initiative and wipe out a part of the them.

265
11:38.830 --> 11:40.230
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

266
11:39.160 --> 11:42.040
Now Xue Yue's Central Army is still on the south bank of the Wujiang River.

267
11:40.350 --> 11:42.280
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

268
11:42.570 --> 11:45.600
The Guizhou Army has just occupied Zunyi and Tongzi,

269
11:45.630 --> 11:47.050
with no intention of going north.

270
11:47.050 --> 11:48.510
Let's fight a battle first

271
11:49.010 --> 11:50.320
to dampen the momentum of the Sichuan Army.

272
11:50.320 --> 11:51.040
Good.

273
11:51.740 --> 11:52.320
Let's go.

274
11:57.480 --> 12:00.000
On January 27, 1935,

275
12:00.680 --> 12:02.960
acting on Mao Zedong's recommendation, the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

276
12:02.960 --> 12:04.040
ordered

277
12:04.410 --> 12:07.650
parts of the 1st and 9th Red Army Corps to block

278
12:07.650 --> 12:10.320
the enemy advancing south from Chishui and Xishui;

279
12:10.320 --> 12:12.410
concentrate the main forces of the 3rd and 5th Red Army Corps

280
12:12.410 --> 12:14.940
along with the Cadre Regiment of the Military Commission Column

281
12:14.940 --> 12:17.700
to build an ambush position at Qinggangpo

282
12:17.730 --> 12:20.760
to encircle and annihilate the four regiments of the Sichuan Army pursuing the Red Army;

283
12:20.760 --> 12:22.150
use the 9th Red Army Corps

284
12:22.150 --> 12:25.100
and the 2nd Division of the 1st Red Army Corps as the reserve force.

285
12:25.100 --> 12:28.460
The battle was under the unified command of Peng Dehuai.

286
12:32.440 --> 12:33.390
Comrades,

287
12:35.440 --> 12:38.840
you have all read the telegraphic order from the Military Commission.

288
12:38.840 --> 12:41.280
As for the combat deployment of each division and regiment,

289
12:41.280 --> 12:44.010
Comrade Deng Ping has also explained it clearly.

290
12:44.010 --> 12:46.550
[Peng Dehuai Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

291
12:44.290 --> 12:47.440
There's just one thing I want to emphasize.

292
12:49.740 --> 12:51.190
Behind us

293
12:51.560 --> 12:53.650
is the Party Central Committee and the Military Commission.

294
12:53.650 --> 12:55.510
Once we fail to hold the position,

295
12:55.890 --> 12:58.080
then the leaders of the Central Committee and the Military Commission

296
12:58.040 --> 13:00.480
[Yang Shangkun, Political Commissar of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

297
12:58.260 --> 13:00.330
will be exposed to the enemy's guns.

298
13:01.130 --> 13:03.720
Our Red Army may be surrounded,

299
13:04.090 --> 13:06.090
suffering another disaster like the Battle of the Xiang River.

300
13:05.990 --> 13:07.580
[Deng Ping, Chief of Staff of 3rd Red Army Corps]

301
13:09.540 --> 13:12.340
So we must win this battle.

302
13:15.170 --> 13:16.080
Any other questions?

303
13:16.080 --> 13:17.050
No questions.

304
13:17.200 --> 13:18.580
We will resolutely complete the task!

305
13:17.670 --> 13:18.500
[Zhong Chibing, Political Commissar of the 5th Division, 3rd Red Army Corps]

306
13:19.620 --> 13:20.860
I have a question!

307
13:24.170 --> 13:26.080
Commander-in-Chief Peng, I have a question.

308
13:25.120 --> 13:27.740
[Chen Geng, head of the Cadre Regiment of the 1st Military Commission Column]

309
13:26.600 --> 13:28.560
I heard you sent the 3rd Corps and 5th Corps

310
13:28.560 --> 13:29.960
to the ambush frontline,

311
13:30.110 --> 13:31.870
and left our Cadre Regiment

312
13:31.890 --> 13:33.950
at Baima Mountain as a reserve force.

313
13:34.200 --> 13:35.600
I think this arrangement

314
13:35.670 --> 13:37.250
treats some of us differently.

315
13:37.250 --> 13:38.200
Chen Geng,

316
13:38.800 --> 13:41.130
The ridgelines at Qinggangpo are only so long.

317
13:41.130 --> 13:43.920
I can't send all our troops charging to the front line.

318
13:43.920 --> 13:45.350
Yes, I know that.

319
13:45.720 --> 13:46.480
But,

320
13:50.900 --> 13:53.110
can you send in our Cadre Regiment

321
13:53.320 --> 13:55.220
and pull the other divisions back?

322
13:55.220 --> 13:57.080
We can't afford to come away empty-handed

323
13:57.080 --> 13:58.130
like we did at Zunyi.

324
13:58.130 --> 13:59.190
Comrade Chen Geng.

325
13:59.410 --> 14:02.480
It will take time for the 9th Corps and the 2nd Division to get into position.

326
14:02.480 --> 14:03.530
Before they arrive,

327
14:03.530 --> 14:04.840
you are the final guarantee

328
14:04.840 --> 14:06.170
for this entire battle.

329
14:06.370 --> 14:07.080
Besides,

330
14:07.960 --> 14:11.320
the Military Commission's command post is right at Baima Mountain.

331
14:11.320 --> 14:12.250
With you here,

332
14:12.720 --> 14:14.390
we feel reassured.

333
14:14.660 --> 14:15.370
Comrade Shangkun.

334
14:15.370 --> 14:16.430
Comrade Chen Geng.

335
14:17.300 --> 14:19.500
Keeping your Cadre Regiment in reserve

336
14:20.100 --> 14:21.630
isn't a slight against you.

337
14:24.080 --> 14:26.130
It's to ensure our victory.

338
14:27.090 --> 14:28.560
This is the first battle we're fighting

339
14:28.560 --> 14:30.160
since the Zunyi Conference.

340
14:33.260 --> 14:34.180
Understood.

341
14:34.410 --> 14:37.470
Our Cadre Regiment stands ready for orders at any time.

342
14:48.140 --> 14:49.060
Comrades,

343
14:50.440 --> 14:51.600
any other questions?

344
14:51.600 --> 14:52.600
No.

345
14:54.410 --> 14:55.770
Prepare for the decisive battle.

346
14:55.770 --> 14:56.560
Yes.

347
14:57.930 --> 14:59.460
How many enemies are there?

348
15:00.650 --> 15:02.050
Where are they?

349
15:03.250 --> 15:04.890
This is the question the leaders care about most

350
15:04.890 --> 15:06.890
on this long journey,

351
15:07.600 --> 15:09.130
and it's also the task the Second Bureau of the Military Commission

352
15:09.130 --> 15:12.560
must accomplish at every moment.

353
15:12.590 --> 15:15.510
This is the most difficult and tense moment

354
15:12.660 --> 15:15.530
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

355
15:15.680 --> 15:17.530
the comrades of the Second Bureau have experienced.

356
15:17.530 --> 15:18.720
The Sichuan Army used a code

357
15:18.720 --> 15:21.450
called "Laiquben" with the codename "Zhengmi".

358
15:21.890 --> 15:24.930
This code completely scrambles the word order.

359
15:25.050 --> 15:27.370
Every word needs to be deciphered individually,

360
15:27.370 --> 15:30.120
which makes the deciphering work extremely slow.

361
15:30.120 --> 15:32.180
The words "enemy situation unknown"

362
15:32.290 --> 15:36.170
hang over everyone's head like a curse.

363
15:56.500 --> 16:01.270
[Central Revolutionary Military Commission Command Post, Baima Mountain Ridge, Tucheng, Guizhou]

364
16:11.560 --> 16:12.860
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

365
16:16.370 --> 16:17.500
Vice Chairman Zhou.

366
16:19.270 --> 16:20.340
I stewed some winter melon soup

367
16:20.340 --> 16:23.000
to help the comrades clear their internal heat.

368
16:33.410 --> 16:34.960
Two, three, five.

369
16:49.010 --> 16:49.530
Zou.

370
16:49.960 --> 16:50.530
Cao.

371
16:50.530 --> 16:51.010
Come here.

372
16:51.010 --> 16:52.090
Vice Chairman Zhou.

373
16:52.090 --> 16:53.350
Bring those mugs over.

374
16:57.610 --> 16:59.800
Let the steam warm your eyes,

375
17:00.440 --> 17:01.940
then apply a hot towel.

376
17:01.970 --> 17:02.880
Okay.

377
17:02.900 --> 17:03.540
Come.

378
17:06.280 --> 17:07.280
Deputy Director.

379
17:10.069 --> 17:11.800
Thank you, Vice Chairman Zhou.

380
17:22.800 --> 17:23.430
Zeng.

381
17:23.450 --> 17:24.310
Don't touch me.

382
17:25.089 --> 17:26.010
Step aside.

383
17:38.330 --> 17:39.590
The Sichuan Army used a type of cipher text

384
17:39.590 --> 17:42.460
commonly known as "Laiquben".

385
17:43.250 --> 17:45.180
This cipher is extremely complex.

386
17:46.440 --> 17:47.440
Every single word

387
17:47.720 --> 17:49.850
needs to be deciphered individually.

388
17:50.080 --> 17:52.760
There is no connection between the words,

389
17:53.200 --> 17:55.080
nor are there any patterns to follow.

390
17:55.080 --> 17:57.160
Moreover, the telegrams

391
17:57.190 --> 17:59.380
contained many repeated numbers,

392
17:59.650 --> 18:02.450
which made them extremely difficult to decipher.

393
18:02.480 --> 18:05.330
To obtain a valid message,

394
18:09.000 --> 18:10.440
we still need some time.

395
18:17.650 --> 18:19.460
Repeated numbers.

396
18:26.730 --> 18:30.680
Try to find a flaw in the repeated numbers.

397
19:25.340 --> 19:29.290
[Sichuan Army Frontline Position, Top of a Battalion, Qinggangpo, Guizhou]

398
19:31.720 --> 19:32.480
Map.

399
19:45.080 --> 19:48.170
[Guo Xunqi, Commander of the Southern Bank Anti-Communist Army Reserve and Commander of the 3rd Brigade, Training Division]

400
19:48.990 --> 19:51.340
Have you discovered something?

401
19:53.420 --> 19:55.550
Qinggangpo's terrain is intriguing,

402
19:56.430 --> 19:57.690
with a valley squeezed

403
19:58.970 --> 20:00.730
between two mountains.

404
20:01.520 --> 20:03.950
Are you worried about an ambush?

405
20:05.170 --> 20:06.610
Aren't you?

406
20:07.440 --> 20:08.090
Staff Officer Zhang.

407
20:08.090 --> 20:08.650
Here.

408
20:08.680 --> 20:09.570
Pass on my orders.

409
20:09.570 --> 20:12.430
The vanguard regiment must avoid the valley floor.

410
20:13.850 --> 20:16.570
Advance along the ridgelines on both sides,

411
20:17.600 --> 20:19.730
seize the high ground along the route,

412
20:20.870 --> 20:22.170
then advance step by step.

413
20:22.170 --> 20:22.680
Yes.

414
20:25.770 --> 20:28.230
Zhu De and Liu Bocheng of the Communist Party

415
20:28.280 --> 20:29.540
are both from Sichuan.

416
20:29.930 --> 20:31.460
If we don't fight them well,

417
20:33.820 --> 20:37.280
I'm afraid we'll be looked down upon by these fellow townsmen.

418
20:39.290 --> 20:41.180
Guo Xunqi ordered the Sichuan army

419
20:41.180 --> 20:43.700
to march along the ridge to seize the hilltop

420
20:43.730 --> 20:45.240
and attack from the flank and rear.

421
20:45.240 --> 20:47.090
The Red Army was forced to abandon its ambush

422
20:47.090 --> 20:49.150
and launch a frontal assault uphill,

423
20:49.340 --> 20:51.790
putting it on the defensive.

424
20:59.420 --> 21:00.570
Report.

425
21:02.270 --> 21:03.500
The Sichuan army didn't take the valley.

426
21:03.500 --> 21:05.330
They seized the high ground along the ridges on both sides

427
21:05.330 --> 21:06.990
and engaged us in a firefight.

428
21:08.000 --> 21:09.760
This Reckless Guo

429
21:09.760 --> 21:11.020
is not reckless at all.

430
21:16.840 --> 21:17.520
Report.

431
21:22.150 --> 21:24.650
The Communist army has ambushes on both sides of the valley.

432
21:24.650 --> 21:25.570
Our vanguard battalion

433
21:25.570 --> 21:27.030
has already engaged them.

434
21:27.090 --> 21:28.330
Where are the Communist army's positions?

435
21:28.330 --> 21:28.930
Here,

436
21:29.170 --> 21:29.610
here,

437
21:29.890 --> 21:30.570
and here.

438
21:30.930 --> 21:32.440
Order the 2nd Battalion of the 7th Regiment

439
21:32.440 --> 21:33.640
to rush to reinforce.

440
21:33.850 --> 21:35.440
Order the outflanking troops to speed up

441
21:35.440 --> 21:36.710
and attack the left wing of the Communist army.

442
21:36.710 --> 21:37.940
The 8th Regiment must speed up,

443
21:37.940 --> 21:39.480
cross the Zhaimen Pass at full speed,

444
21:39.480 --> 21:40.850
and cut off the Communist army's defense line.

445
21:40.850 --> 21:43.090
The rest of the troops will advance towards their positions

446
21:43.090 --> 21:44.370
with all their might.

447
21:44.570 --> 21:46.280
Any officer or soldier who dares to retreat half a step

448
21:46.280 --> 21:47.280
will be dealt with by military law.

449
21:47.280 --> 21:48.280
Yes, sir.

450
21:49.130 --> 21:50.690
Set up the command post at Yong'an Temple.

451
21:50.690 --> 21:54.000
Send someone immediately to notify Brigade Commander Pan Zuo in the rear,

452
21:54.000 --> 21:55.800
and ask him to lead his troops immediately

453
21:55.800 --> 21:57.370
to come up and assist in the attack.

454
21:57.370 --> 21:59.030
Also, send an urgent telegram to Commander Liao

455
21:59.030 --> 22:00.280
of the Model Division's 3rd Brigade,

456
22:00.280 --> 22:02.740
asking him to rush to reinforce Qinggangpo.

457
22:03.120 --> 22:03.990
It must be urgent.

458
22:03.990 --> 22:04.820
Yes, sir.

459
22:04.850 --> 22:07.110
Confidential Section, send a telegram.

460
23:04.130 --> 23:05.860
Commander Peng, wait a moment.

461
23:07.570 --> 23:08.700
Commander Peng said

462
23:08.930 --> 23:10.960
the Sichuan Army isn't following the expected playbook.

463
23:10.960 --> 23:13.490
Our previous preset positions are useless.

464
23:14.100 --> 23:15.760
The ambush has turned into a flank attack.

465
23:15.760 --> 23:17.230
The enemy's offensive is very fierce,

466
23:17.230 --> 23:19.530
which is completely beyond our expectations.

467
23:19.530 --> 23:21.460
This Guo Xunqi is quite something.

468
23:25.170 --> 23:26.100
Peng Dehuai,

469
23:26.520 --> 23:27.520
this is Zhu De.

470
23:27.930 --> 23:30.260
Tell the comrades of the 3rd and 5th Corps,

471
23:30.640 --> 23:32.560
no matter how fierce the enemy is,

472
23:33.330 --> 23:35.480
we must resolutely suppress them.

473
23:35.830 --> 23:37.290
Please rest assured, Commander-in-Chief.

474
23:37.290 --> 23:39.690
We will defend the position with our lives.

475
23:41.390 --> 23:42.280
Bocheng,

476
23:42.720 --> 23:44.360
where are the 9th Corps and the 2nd Red Division

477
23:44.360 --> 23:45.360
now?

478
23:45.850 --> 23:47.370
The 9th Corps is having trouble with the terrain

479
23:47.370 --> 23:50.030
and may not reach its assigned position in time.

480
23:50.050 --> 23:51.360
The 2nd Red Division is accelerating its advance,

481
23:51.360 --> 23:53.820
but it will take at least two hours to arrive.

482
23:54.650 --> 23:56.000
The Sichuan Army has now activated

483
23:56.000 --> 23:57.130
a new cipher system.

484
23:57.170 --> 23:59.440
Every word needs to be cracked individually.

485
23:59.440 --> 24:01.010
There is still no progress.

486
24:19.980 --> 24:20.930
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff of the 2nd Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

487
24:35.600 --> 24:36.530
Report.

488
24:43.400 --> 24:46.050
I brought some boiled water for the leaders.

489
25:54.050 --> 25:54.810
Chen Geng.

490
25:56.610 --> 25:58.170
Go back and wait for orders.

491
25:59.540 --> 26:00.430
Go.

492
26:00.970 --> 26:01.730
Yes.

493
26:16.600 --> 26:17.410
Mao,

494
26:18.290 --> 26:19.890
what are you thinking about?

495
26:24.060 --> 26:27.020
The Sichuan army is acting out of character.

496
26:27.990 --> 26:29.990
They must have something to rely on.

497
27:00.930 --> 27:02.260
Brigade Commander Guo.

498
27:03.200 --> 27:04.520
Where is Brigade Commander Guo?

499
27:04.520 --> 27:05.410
Rubi,

500
27:05.440 --> 27:06.570
you arrived so fast.

501
27:07.720 --> 27:09.130
Orders are strict. How dare I delay?

502
27:09.040 --> 27:12.090
[Pan Zuo, Commander of the Independent 4th Brigade, Southern Bank Anti-Communist Army Reserve]

503
27:09.330 --> 27:10.520
Not only have I arrived,

504
27:10.520 --> 27:12.410
but my three regiments have also followed your deployment

505
27:12.410 --> 27:13.440
and pressed forward.

506
27:13.440 --> 27:13.930
Great.

507
27:14.040 --> 27:14.810
Come.

508
27:14.960 --> 27:16.480
With your two brigades, six regiments in all,

509
27:16.480 --> 27:19.610
plus Commander Liao's three regiments arriving later,

510
27:21.520 --> 27:22.440
we just need to pin down

511
27:22.440 --> 27:24.200
Zhu and Mao's main force here.

512
27:24.410 --> 27:26.140
The main army will be here soon,

513
27:26.240 --> 27:28.170
and the Communists won't escape us.

514
27:28.170 --> 27:28.890
Good.

515
27:29.040 --> 27:30.110
Let's go check the position.

516
27:30.110 --> 27:31.150
Let's go.

517
28:51.890 --> 28:53.240
We cannot lose the position.

518
28:53.240 --> 28:54.890
I know you are fighting hard.

519
28:55.330 --> 28:56.720
But the other divisions are under

520
28:56.720 --> 28:57.980
just as much pressure.

521
28:58.280 --> 29:00.440
You must not lose your position.

522
29:00.930 --> 29:01.810
Chief of Staff,

523
29:02.000 --> 29:03.170
I didn't call you here just to complain

524
29:03.170 --> 29:05.170
about our difficulties or ask for reinforcements.

525
29:05.170 --> 29:07.170
I'm telling you something is wrong.

526
29:07.440 --> 29:09.330
If the enemy only had four Regiments,

527
29:09.330 --> 29:10.130
there shouldn't be

528
29:10.130 --> 29:12.280
this many Sichuan troops on our front.

529
29:12.520 --> 29:14.480
They keep swarming in like a nest of hornets.

530
29:14.480 --> 29:15.850
They are everywhere.

531
29:19.220 --> 29:20.440
How are we supposed to fight like this?

532
29:20.440 --> 29:22.440
Why are there more and more enemies?

533
29:24.200 --> 29:25.260
Fight to the death!

534
29:25.410 --> 29:26.040
Yes.

535
29:26.080 --> 29:27.160
Charge!

536
29:30.200 --> 29:32.160
Hello? Hello?

537
29:39.480 --> 29:40.350
Messenger!

538
29:40.370 --> 29:40.810
Here!

539
29:40.930 --> 29:41.650
Messenger!

540
29:41.850 --> 29:42.680
Here!

541
29:42.930 --> 29:44.590
Run and notify all Regiments.

542
29:44.610 --> 29:45.610
Do not let a single enemy

543
29:45.610 --> 29:46.850
pass through our position alive.

544
29:46.850 --> 29:48.170
-Go! -Yes.

545
29:52.200 --> 29:53.590
Comrades on the front line

546
29:53.590 --> 29:55.150
also report that the enemy numbers don't add up.

547
29:55.150 --> 29:57.280
Based on the reports from all Divisions,

548
29:57.280 --> 29:59.280
the enemy has at least 6 or 7 Regiments.

549
29:59.280 --> 30:00.720
That's over 12,000 men.

550
30:00.850 --> 30:02.380
The intelligence is wrong.

551
30:02.570 --> 30:03.570
What's going on?

552
30:05.190 --> 30:05.990
Report!

553
30:06.130 --> 30:07.240
More than a Regiment of Sichuan troops

554
30:07.240 --> 30:08.400
has broken through the 5th Corps' defense line.

555
30:08.400 --> 30:10.000
They've reached Loufengya.

556
30:10.520 --> 30:12.680
Beyond Loufengya lies the Military Commission's command post.

557
30:12.680 --> 30:13.890
Further ahead is the Chishui River,

558
30:13.890 --> 30:15.750
There's no natural defense left.

559
30:20.060 --> 30:22.300
We must seal that breach.

560
30:22.550 --> 30:24.280
We can't spare any more troops.

561
30:27.950 --> 30:29.280
Connect to the Military Commission.

562
30:29.280 --> 30:30.240
Connect to the Military Commission.

563
30:30.240 --> 30:30.810
Yes.

564
30:38.690 --> 30:41.520
Okay, I understand.

565
30:44.650 --> 30:48.460
Comrade Peng Dehuai requests that we retreat as soon as possible.

566
30:49.310 --> 30:50.180
Retreat?

567
30:51.970 --> 30:53.490
Where to?

568
30:55.520 --> 30:57.050
We have nowhere to retreat.

569
30:57.440 --> 30:58.680
Right now, the 3rd and 5th Corps

570
30:58.680 --> 31:00.480
have used all available troops.

571
31:01.040 --> 31:03.090
The 9th Corps definitely won't make it.

572
31:03.090 --> 31:04.480
The 2nd Division won't arrive

573
31:04.480 --> 31:05.940
for at least another hour.

574
31:07.410 --> 31:08.130
Chen Geng!

575
31:08.440 --> 31:09.410
Here!

576
31:11.090 --> 31:11.720
Send the Cadre Regiment.

577
31:11.720 --> 31:12.570
Yes.

578
31:12.760 --> 31:14.360
The Cadre Regiment is ready.

579
31:14.440 --> 31:15.410
Please rest assured, leader.

580
31:15.410 --> 31:17.810
We will resolutely repel the enemy and retake the position.

581
31:17.810 --> 31:19.670
One Cadre Regiment is not enough.

582
31:21.090 --> 31:23.090
Commander-in-Chief, do you have any other troops available?

583
31:23.090 --> 31:24.690
There is also an old soldier.

584
31:25.480 --> 31:27.650
I, Zhu De, will lead the Cadre Regiment up

585
31:27.650 --> 31:28.720
to command at the front.

586
31:28.720 --> 31:29.370
No, no, no.

587
31:29.480 --> 31:31.090
You don't need a cannon to kill a mosquito.

588
31:31.090 --> 31:31.850
Chen Geng.

589
31:32.130 --> 31:33.290
Go assemble your troops.

590
31:33.290 --> 31:34.120
Yes.

591
31:34.140 --> 31:36.140
The Commander-in-Chief cannot go.

592
31:41.410 --> 31:42.330
Comrade Zhu De.

593
31:42.610 --> 31:43.990
How can the Commander-in-Chief go to the front?

594
31:43.990 --> 31:44.940
You must stay.

595
31:44.960 --> 31:47.130
Commander-in-Chief, I am the Chief of Staff.

596
31:47.130 --> 31:47.930
According to convention,

597
31:47.930 --> 31:50.330
I should be the one to command at the front at this time.

598
31:50.330 --> 31:51.000
You stay.

599
31:51.310 --> 31:52.520
Liu Bocheng, stop right there.

600
31:52.520 --> 31:54.000
Commander-in-Chief, I must go.

601
31:54.000 --> 31:55.720
Don't worry about my safety!

602
31:58.640 --> 32:01.570
It's enough to have Mao and Enlai holding the fort here.

603
32:01.570 --> 32:02.630
If I go to the front,

604
32:02.890 --> 32:03.890
I can boost morale

605
32:03.960 --> 32:05.690
and make decisions on the spot.

606
32:06.240 --> 32:07.230
Commander-in-Chief Zhu.

607
32:07.230 --> 32:08.590
No, absolutely not.

608
32:10.120 --> 32:10.810
No.

609
32:13.230 --> 32:14.760
If anything happens to you,

610
32:15.020 --> 32:18.150
we won't be able to explain it to the whole Party and army.

611
32:18.400 --> 32:19.360
Mao.

612
32:20.290 --> 32:22.890
This is the first battle after the Zunyi Conference.

613
32:22.890 --> 32:25.240
Any cloud in the sky can bring rain.

614
32:25.610 --> 32:27.950
If the Zunyi Conference opens up a new chapter for us,

615
32:27.950 --> 32:30.560
what does it matter if I die?

616
32:31.090 --> 32:32.480
No, absolutely not.

617
32:33.000 --> 32:34.520
The Kuomintang newspapers said

618
32:34.520 --> 32:36.370
that I was killed.

619
32:36.830 --> 32:38.290
Aren't I still alive and well?

620
32:38.290 --> 32:40.160
No, absolutely not.

621
32:51.360 --> 32:52.810
Don't worry, old friend.

622
32:53.210 --> 32:56.610
The enemy's bullets can't hit me.

623
33:23.600 --> 33:24.690
Mao.

624
33:25.280 --> 33:26.930
"They adorn these mountains,

625
33:26.930 --> 33:28.120
making them look even better today."

626
33:28.120 --> 33:28.850
Good.

627
33:29.410 --> 33:31.990
Commander-in-Chief, I'll stay by your side and observe the battle.

628
33:31.990 --> 33:32.520
Good.

629
35:57.860 --> 36:00.640
Comrades, Commander-in-Chief Zhu has arrived at the front.

630
36:00.640 --> 36:02.900
The Cadre Regiment is up. Charge with me!

631
36:03.210 --> 36:05.440
Charge! Charge!

632
37:14.600 --> 37:15.330
Good.

633
37:16.480 --> 37:18.400
The Commander-in-Chief turned the tide.

634
37:18.400 --> 37:20.090
Chen Geng can be a Commander.

635
37:23.560 --> 37:24.690
Vice Chairman Zhou.

636
37:25.020 --> 37:25.940
Chairman Mao.

637
37:26.520 --> 37:28.330
The Red 2nd Division has arrived.

638
37:28.330 --> 37:29.210
Great.

639
37:29.850 --> 37:32.080
Order them to rush to the front immediately,

640
37:32.080 --> 37:33.600
directly under the command of the Commander-in-Chief.

641
37:33.600 --> 37:34.250
Yes.

642
37:47.330 --> 37:48.000
Commander-in-Chief.

643
37:48.000 --> 37:48.860
Chief of Staff.

644
37:48.960 --> 37:49.690
Why are you here?

645
37:49.690 --> 37:50.640
I know what you're going to say.

646
37:50.640 --> 37:51.640
Save your breath.

647
37:52.350 --> 37:53.810
What's the situation now?

648
37:54.340 --> 37:55.440
The Cadre Regiment

649
37:55.690 --> 37:56.960
has sealed the breach,

650
37:57.480 --> 38:00.140
and the 2nd Division has taken up its positions.

651
38:00.550 --> 38:03.000
We've temporarily halted the enemy's advance,

652
38:03.000 --> 38:05.330
and both sides are now locked in a standoff.

653
38:05.330 --> 38:06.560
Is the Sichuan army still not retreating?

654
38:06.560 --> 38:07.160
No.

655
38:07.820 --> 38:09.950
It seems we underestimated the enemy.

656
38:21.040 --> 38:21.920
Decoded!

657
38:22.890 --> 38:23.640
Qian!

658
38:25.210 --> 38:25.960
It's done.

659
38:30.130 --> 38:30.960
Zeng, Zeng.

660
38:34.850 --> 38:35.690
Zeng, Zeng.

661
38:35.720 --> 38:36.280
Zeng.

662
38:36.470 --> 38:37.870
Zeng, come, get up, Zeng.

663
38:38.960 --> 38:39.620
This is bad.

664
38:43.040 --> 38:45.730
Vice Chairman Zhou sat behind you

665
38:46.030 --> 38:47.110
all night.

666
38:48.640 --> 38:50.440
Apply a hot towel to him.

667
38:50.640 --> 38:51.440
Okay.

668
38:51.550 --> 38:52.750
Lie down first, Zeng.

669
38:53.160 --> 38:53.800
Here.

670
38:53.900 --> 38:56.310
I'm fine. I'm fine.

671
38:56.690 --> 38:57.960
I've been sitting for over ten hours.

672
38:57.960 --> 38:59.080
My butt is numb.

673
38:59.240 --> 39:01.040
You guys go about your business.

674
39:01.830 --> 39:02.580
It's fine.

675
39:02.640 --> 39:04.000
I just need to move around a bit.

676
39:04.000 --> 39:04.660
Here, Zeng.

677
39:05.080 --> 39:06.080
Apply this first.

678
39:06.250 --> 39:06.730
Okay.

679
39:14.480 --> 39:15.480
Here, Zeng.

680
39:15.810 --> 39:18.530
This is winter melon soup sent by Vice Chairman Zhou.

681
39:18.530 --> 39:19.530
Drink some first.

682
39:20.440 --> 39:21.560
Vice Chairman Zhou

683
39:22.480 --> 39:24.890
sat behind me all night?

684
39:25.080 --> 39:25.960
Exactly.

685
39:27.250 --> 39:28.290
Why didn't I know?

686
39:29.850 --> 39:31.290
You should have told me.

687
40:09.520 --> 40:10.330
Chairman Mao.

688
40:10.560 --> 40:11.690
Vice Chairman Zhou.

689
40:12.680 --> 40:13.690
Vice Chairman Zhou.

690
40:13.690 --> 40:14.410
Zhuangfei.

691
40:15.430 --> 40:18.230
The Sichuan army's telegram has been deciphered.

692
40:18.730 --> 40:21.370
The Sichuan Army facing us doesn't have 4 regiments,

693
40:21.370 --> 40:22.250
but 6.

694
40:22.520 --> 40:24.730
Plus the 3 Regiments of the Independent 3rd Brigade,

695
40:24.730 --> 40:26.290
and the subsequent reinforcements,

696
40:26.290 --> 40:29.950
the total strength of the Sichuan army is no less than 9 Regiments.

697
40:32.020 --> 40:33.350
We can't fight anymore.

698
40:34.480 --> 40:35.730
Convene everyone immediately

699
40:35.730 --> 40:37.190
for an emergency meeting.

700
40:44.230 --> 40:48.960
[Central Revolutionary Military Commission Command Post, Baima Mountain Ridge, Tucheng, Guizhou]

701
40:44.820 --> 40:45.820
Comrades.

702
40:46.210 --> 40:48.210
The current situation is very critical.

703
40:48.210 --> 40:49.520
We need to make a decision as soon as possible.

704
40:49.520 --> 40:50.930
If you have any opinions or suggestions,

705
40:50.930 --> 40:51.960
please bring them up quickly.

706
40:51.850 --> 40:53.840
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

707
40:56.640 --> 40:59.700
The Zunyi area has been reoccupied by the Guizhou Army.

708
41:00.040 --> 41:02.300
And we failed to capture Chishui County.

709
41:02.700 --> 41:04.900
We can neither advance nor retreat now.

710
41:05.410 --> 41:07.040
Besides continuing to fight,

711
41:07.040 --> 41:08.960
do we have any other options?

712
41:09.100 --> 41:11.150
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee and Political Commissar of the Military Commission Column]

713
41:09.440 --> 41:11.850
But our previous intelligence on the enemy was wrong.

714
41:11.850 --> 41:13.830
Now the enemy outnumbers us several times over.

715
41:13.830 --> 41:14.890
Perhaps even more enemies

716
41:14.890 --> 41:16.290
are swarming towards us.

717
41:16.640 --> 41:18.300
If we keep fighting like this,

718
41:18.370 --> 41:20.480
our situation will only get worse.

719
41:20.510 --> 41:21.200
Yes.

720
41:21.600 --> 41:22.720
If we keep fighting like this,

721
41:22.720 --> 41:25.520
it will become a seesaw battle, a war of attrition.

722
41:28.160 --> 41:31.380
[Kai Feng (He Kequan), Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee,]

723
41:30.520 --> 41:31.650
Comrade Mao Zedong.

724
41:31.890 --> 41:32.960
You are now Comrade Enlai's

725
41:32.960 --> 41:34.370
military assistant.

726
41:34.750 --> 41:37.110
You need to play your role at this time.

727
41:41.210 --> 41:43.480
I agree with Enlai's judgment just now.

728
41:43.960 --> 41:46.570
We can't fight a seesaw battle or a war of attrition with the enemy.

729
41:46.570 --> 41:48.520
We should withdraw from the battle immediately.

730
41:48.520 --> 41:49.210
Withdraw?

731
41:50.190 --> 41:50.900
Yes.

732
41:52.370 --> 41:54.890
We must first withdraw to

733
41:55.120 --> 41:57.580
the southern area of Gulin to seek mobility.

734
41:57.640 --> 41:58.850
How can we withdraw?

735
42:07.170 --> 42:10.560
Cross the Chishui River westward from Tucheng.

736
42:14.810 --> 42:15.740
Comrade Zedong.

737
42:16.160 --> 42:17.930
Do you mean to change the original plan

738
42:17.930 --> 42:19.760
of crossing the river north from Chishui?

739
42:19.760 --> 42:20.390
Yes.

740
42:20.680 --> 42:22.330
How can an established military plan

741
42:22.330 --> 42:23.790
be changed just like that?

742
42:23.850 --> 42:26.120
No battle plan is set in stone.

743
42:26.250 --> 42:27.160
Flexibility

744
42:27.600 --> 42:28.920
is to shake off passivity

745
42:28.920 --> 42:30.320
and gain the initiative.

746
42:35.640 --> 42:36.680
I agree.

747
42:41.180 --> 42:43.580
I agree with Comrade Mao Zedong's opinion.

748
42:45.490 --> 42:48.020
I hope the tragedy of the Battle of Xiang River

749
42:49.890 --> 42:51.090
will not be repeated.

750
43:00.950 --> 43:01.800
Agreed.

751
43:02.410 --> 43:03.160
Agreed.

752
43:03.290 --> 43:04.210
Agreed.
